{"id":34051,"slug":"saint-omer","title":"Saint Omer","year":2022,"country":"France","duration":123,"spine":1212,"url":"https://www.criterion.com/films/34051-saint-omer","cover":"https://s3.amazonaws.com/criterion-production/films/1baad8b7d5dc29744cbd262d1502b8b7/7nslycY8VgPrwkyYP9YWsAIRwStlxs_large.jpg","description":"Bringing a documentarian’s sense of open-ended inquiry to her first narrative feature, writer-director Alice Diop constructs a morally and emotionally layered courtroom drama unlike any other. When she travels to Saint-Omer, France, to attend the trial of a young Senegalese woman (Guslagie Malanda) accused of murdering her infant daughter, novelist Rama (Kayije Kagame) finds herself shaken to the core by a case that proves to have profound resonances with her own life. Interweaving complex themes of mother-daughter bonds, immigrant alienation, and postcolonial trauma into a piercing portrait of two mysteriously connected women, Diop forgoes mere questions of guilt and innocence in order to plumb the unsettling unknowability of the human soul.","boxset":0,"scraped":1,"directors":[{"name":"Alice Diop","slug":"alice-diop"}],"cast":[{"actor":"Kayije Kagame","role":"Rama","slug":"kayije-kagame"},{"actor":"Guslagie Malanda","role":"Laurence Coly","slug":"guslagie-malanda"},{"actor":"Valérie Dréville","role":"Investigating judge","slug":"valerie-dreville"},{"actor":"Aurélia Petit","role":"Councilor Vaudenay","slug":"aurelia-petit"},{"actor":"Xavier Maly","role":"Luc Dumontet","slug":"xavier-maly"},{"actor":"Robert Cantarella","role":"Prosecuting attorney","slug":"robert-cantarella"},{"actor":"Salimata Kamate","role":"Odile Diatta","slug":"salimata-kamate"},{"actor":"Thomas de Pourquery","role":"Adrien","slug":"thomas-de-pourquery"}],"credits":[{"role":"Director","person":"Alice Diop","slug":"alice-diop"},{"role":"Written by","person":"Alice Diop","slug":"alice-diop"},{"role":"Written by","person":"Amrita David","slug":null},{"role":"Written by","person":"Mari